  "checked": "First-season league titles: Cantona (joined Nov 1992, champion 1992-93), Drogba 2004-05, Kante 2015-16, Haaland 2022-23; Henry, Ronaldo, De Bruyne, Salah, Van Dijk, Rodri waited (Wikipedia champions list). PL Player of the Season since 1994-95: Kante 2016-17, Haaland 2022-23; never Cantona or Drogba (Wikipedia, FourFourTwo). 2015-16 table Leicester 81, Arsenal 71, Spurs 70, City 66, United 66 (Wikipedia 2015-16 PL); 5000-1 at the start (BBC). Fees: Cantona about 1.2m, Drogba about 24m, Kante about 5.6m (Sky, ESPN), Haaland about 51m (Wikipedia). Kante 175 tackles 2015-16, 31 more than anyone (premierleague.com, FourFourTwo). PFA and FWA 2017 (PFA, FourFourTwo). First player since Cantona to win back-to-back English titles with different clubs; goalkeeper Schwarzer also did, hence 'outfield' (Sport360, Newsletter). Kante's goal in Chelsea 4-0 United, 23 Oct 2016, 70': ran onto Pedro's flick, low finish past De Gea (Sports Mole, premierleague.com). United's kit that day not found: home red assumed (no clash with blue).",
